-- title:
--   Two-variable power series presentation of widehat R over O[[t]]/(t-varpi)
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, let $\varpi \in O$ be irreducible, and let $R$ be a commutative noetherian local $O$-algebra. Let $g, h \in R$, and assume that the maximal ideal of $R$ is the ideal generated by the three elements $\varpi \cdot 1_R$ (the image of $\varpi$ under the structure map $O \to R$), $g$ and $h$, and that the composite $O \to R \to R/\mathfrak m_R$ of the structure map with the residue map is surjective. Write $W := O[[X]]/(X - C(\varpi))$ for the quotient of the one-variable power series ring over $O$ by the ideal generated by $X - C(\varpi)$, and let $\widehat R$ denote the $\mathfrak m_R$-adic completion of $R$, with its canonical map from $R$. Then there exist ring homomorphisms $\theta_W \colon W \to \widehat R$ and $\theta \colon W[[X_0, X_1]] \to \widehat R$, the source of $\theta$ being the power series ring over $W$ in the two variables indexed by `Fin 2`, such that: $\theta_W$ sends the class of the constant series $C(o)$ to the image in $\widehat R$ of $o \cdot 1_R$ for every $o \in O$; $\theta_W$ sends the class of $X$ to the image of $\varpi \cdot 1_R$; $\theta$ is surjective; the restriction of $\theta$ to constants, i.e. $\theta$ composed after the coefficient inclusion $W \to W[[X_0,X_1]]$, equals $\theta_W$; and $\theta(X_0)$, $\theta(X_1)$ are the images of $g$, $h$ in $\widehat R$.
--
--   This is the abstract complete-Nakayama presentation of a completed noetherian local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by a uniformiser of the base discrete valuation ring together with two further elements: the completion is exhibited as a quotient of a two-variable power series ring over the coefficient ring $W = O[[X]]/(X - C(\varpi))$. It underlies the local descriptions of crossing and node models, being used in the identifications of adic completions of local rings at crossing points with quotients of the $uv$-crossing model.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_exists_surjective_mvPowerSeries_adicCompletion_of_maximalIdeal_eq_span.lean

